# apps/web/.local.env — web-specific env for the local stage.
# Same file structure applies to .dev.env / .prod.env (synced to GitHub
# Secrets via `pnpm sync:secrets`). See docs/deploy.md.
#
# Control-plane secrets (CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, CLOUDFLARE_EMAIL,
# ALCHEMY_STATE_TOKEN) live in `.alchemy.env` at the repo root, NOT here.

# ─── Custom domains (optional; zone must be on Cloudflare DNS) ───
# Only honored for stages `dev` and `prod`. PR previews always use *.workers.dev.
# WEB_DOMAIN=app.example.com
# SERVER_DOMAIN=api.example.com
#
# Alias hostnames that should 301-redirect to WEB_DOMAIN. Comma-separated.
# alchemy creates the proxied DNS records + Cloudflare Single Redirect rules
# automatically — no dashboard work. WEB_DOMAIN must equal its zone name
# (i.e. the apex) for zone lookup to succeed.
# WEB_DOMAIN_ALIASES=www.example.com

# ─── Client-bundle env (visible in browser, never put secrets here) ───
# Inlined into the client bundle at build time by vite-plugin-environment.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL is auto-derived from SERVER_DOMAIN — only set it
# explicitly to override.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=
